course: dictionary
lesson: 642
title: Backwater: a calm place away from the rush
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A backwater is a part of a river where the water is still or slow, away from the main current. Picture a calm pool beside a bend, where the fast river seems far away.
explain: The word can also describe a quiet place where not much happens. The clues are in the sentence: «Then they turn into a quiet backwater by a weir and an old mill.» Quiet and turn into show the boat leaves the busy river for somewhere calm.
explain: Read carefully: a backwater is not just any river. In the story, Ratty and Mole row up a backwater among the reeds, and the water stays calm. In everyday talk, calling a town a backwater means it is dull and slow to change, which can be unkind.
fact: A backwater is a still or slow part of a river, away from the main current.
fact: A weir is a low wall across a river that water tumbles over.
fact: In a calm backwater, mud settles and plants can grow.
fact: Backwater can also mean a quiet place where new ideas arrive slowly.
fact: Calling a town a backwater can be unkind, because it suggests it is dull or old-fashioned.
exercise: «Then they turn into a quiet backwater by a weir and an old mill.» Is a backwater fast or calm? | Full of waves | Fast and rushing | *Calm | Hot and dry
exercise: What is a weir? | *A low wall across a river that water tumbles over | A tall tower by the sea | A kind of bridge for cars | A boat with a sail
exercise: «The Otter says he came to the backwater for a moment's peace.» What does the Otter want? | To sell fish | *Quiet and rest | To be noticed by a crowd | A big race
test: Why might someone call a town a backwater? | *Because it is dull and slow to change | Because it is famous for music festivals | Because it has a big harbour and many ships | Because it is on the top of a mountain
test: Which word in «a restless dripping mill-wheel» is the opposite of the calm you find in a backwater? | mill | *restless | dripping | wheel
exam: In «a restless dripping mill-wheel», what does restless suggest? | Made of stone | Sleeping soundly | Painted red | *Always moving and unable to keep still
